        "date": "2026-11-24T05:25:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(contour): ramp the wall side of a contour along the lead-in and ring\n\nA 2D Contour with side outside (or auto) and entry ramp or helix no longer\ndives straight down at the lead-in. It zig-zags down along the lead-in and\nthe ring at the ramp angle, on every level. Every point lies on the path\nthat the level cuts at full depth, so no chord over the grown region is\nneeded. A helix stands down to the same ramp and says so once. A tabbed\nlevel, or a path too short for the angle, still grazes, named.\n\nFixes #3829\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
